        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Note alternatives to Emscripten in C to Wasm guide]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44351</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44351"/>
        <updated>2026-06-04T01:29:51.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #20177.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1357608893" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20177" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/20177/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20177">#20177</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The guide only mentions Emscripten, which led to the request for a pointer to lighter, more portable alternatives. Per the discussion on the issue (<a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Josh-Cena">@Josh-Cena</a> and <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/bsmth/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/bsmth">@bsmth</a>), the consensus was to keep the tutorial primarily Emscripten-based but add a note about alternatives in the introduction — so this adds a short note pointing to compiling C directly with Clang/LLVM or the WASI SDK, while noting what Emscripten provides that those don't (libc, file system, and other OS emulation).</p>
<p dir="auto">The Clang/LLVM reference is the <a href="https://surma.dev/things/c-to-webassembly/" rel="nofollow">surma.dev write-up</a> <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/bsmth/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/bsmth">@bsmth</a> linked in the thread.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>vamshikrishnaramasamy</name>
            <email>vamshikrishnaramasamy@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/vamshikrishnaramasamy</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-06-04T01:28:08.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify that deleteDatabase() blocks until open connections close]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44350</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44350"/>
        <updated>2026-06-04T01:25:19.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #20368.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1363933918" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20368" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/20368/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20368">#20368</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The page mentions that open connections receive a <code class="notranslate">versionchange</code> event, but doesn't explain the consequence: the deletion will not complete (and <code class="notranslate">success</code> will not fire) while any connection to the database is still open. This is a common source of confusion — people wait for <code class="notranslate">onsuccess</code> that never comes because a connection is left open.</p>
<p dir="auto">This expands the existing sentence to spell out that:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>the deletion stays pending until every connection closes;</li>
<li>a <code class="notranslate">blocked</code> event is fired on the request if a connection doesn't close in response to <code class="notranslate">versionchange</code>;</li>
<li>closing connections (e.g. via <code class="notranslate">IDBDatabase.close()</code>) lets the deletion proceed.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This matches the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#delete-a-database" rel="nofollow">spec's database-deletion steps</a> and the behavior <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/evanstade/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/evanstade">@evanstade</a> quoted on the issue.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>vamshikrishnaramasamy</name>
            <email>vamshikrishnaramasamy@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/vamshikrishnaramasamy</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-06-04T01:23:50.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Note that Attr.isConnected is always false]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44349</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44349"/>
        <updated>2026-06-04T01:24:22.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #42933.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3860235982" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42933" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42933/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42933">#42933</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">isConnected</code> always returns <code class="notranslate">false</code> on an {{domxref("Attr")}} node, even when the attribute's <code class="notranslate">ownerElement</code> is connected to the document. This trips people up, so this adds a note explaining why.</p>
<p dir="auto">As <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/caugner/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/caugner">@caugner</a> noted on the issue, this is consistent across Chrome, Firefox, and Safari, and is out of scope for BCD — the spec defines <code class="notranslate">isConnected</code> for all nodes, and since an attribute node has no parent, it has no root that is a document, so it is never "connected".</p>
<p dir="auto">I confirmed the behavior in Chrome:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const el = document.createElement(&quot;div&quot;);
el.setAttribute(&quot;data-x&quot;, &quot;1&quot;);
const attr = el.getAttributeNode(&quot;data-x&quot;);
document.body.appendChild(el);

